# Studio seats (Idle Party)

One owner + agents. **Six chairs.** Do not invent Lead/Scrum/Network/UA
departments. Do not role-play a panel in chat. On a fork: **one** decision.
Name the winning chair in at most one sentence if the owner would be confused.
Skip this file for routine implement / analyze / commit.

## Chairs

| Chair | Owns | Veto / stop |
|-------|------|-------------|
| **Executive Producer** | Scope, `GROWTH_MANDATE.md` principles, deadlines | Unprompted scope creep; iOS; whale/gacha; weaken hard locks |
| **Game Director** | Loops, SpatialCombat, progression, kits | Second sim; ship with DPS **HIGH**; broken fight |
| **UX Director** | Hub/menus, placement map, readability | Second visual chaos; broken findability |
| **Technical Director** | Architecture, crashes, analyze, save | Red analyze/tests; known crash; god-object as the batch |
| **Art Director** | Kenney/custom, doll, listing **icon** | Foreign dumps; listing shots that are not live combat |
| **Marketing** | Play listing honesty, reviews, ASO | GitHub Releases as funnel; listing that lies |

Owner wins when they name the goal.

## Reports (this studio)

EP over every director. Game Director owns all design hats (systems, combat,
level, economy). UX Director owns UI + UX. Art Director owns all art hats.
Technical Director owns all code + QA-as-tests. Marketing owns community/UA
when relevant. Audio is not a standing chair (Tech + Art when audio files
change). No Scrum Master / PM layer.

## Weight (no standing program)

What to **build:** whatever the owner names (or a clear batch). Do not restore
AL20 hub polish as the default. Game Director may freshen pack mix / boss
tells against play notes. Art sits unless listing conversion is the hole.
Tech never picks the feature unprompted.

## When the owner names more endgame

Prefer deepening **KEY / Gauntlet / Rift / GR / Ashen** unless they name a
new zone, class, or hunt.
